WEBVTT

NOTE Tube Scan Plan — Normal Beam TCG Calibration (condensed)
NOTE Language: English (en)
NOTE Source: Rachel narration via ElevenLabs eleven_multilingual_v2

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.500
TCG Calibration for Normal Beam.

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.300
A step-by-step tutorial.

3
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.000
Step 1.

4
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.500
From the ScanMaster Wizard,
click Teach In.

5
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.500
The Setup Toolbox opens.

6
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.070
Set material velocity, range,
and water path.

7
00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:14.800
Step 2.

8
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.500
Open the TCG tab.

9
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.840
Verify three checkboxes:
Active, Visible, and Drag.

10
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.500
Step 3.

11
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.500
Move the probe to the first F.B.H.,
the near standard.

12
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.530
Drag the yellow dot
onto the response peak.

13
00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:30.500
Step 4.

14
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.000
Adjust the Gain so the F.B.H.
amplitude reaches 80% F.S.H.

15
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.440
Then save. Point one is locked.

16
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.000
Step 5.

17
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.500
Move to the second F.B.H.,
the middle standard.

18
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.970
Drag, gain to 80%, and save.

19
00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:45.500
Step 6.

20
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.500
Move to the third F.B.H.,
the far standard.

21
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.120
All three reference points are now set.

22
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:52.700
Step 7.

23
00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.500
Click the Files tab,
then under TCG, click Save.

24
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.890
Name the file with probe type,
F.B.H. size, and today's date.

25
00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:00.500
Step 8. Important reminder.

26
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.700
Keep the water path
within ± ¼ inch.

27
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.380
Recalibrate after any probe
or material change.

28
00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.500
Calibration complete.

29
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.500
Your TCG curve is ready.
All three F.B.H. responses

30
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.500
are equalized at 80% F.S.H.

31
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.500
Run your inspection.
